This is the most logical and compelling solution I have seen yet.

Perhaps even worse consequences of the profession might acrue.  Like a wizard
might start out with a very high constitution, and see it steadily *decline*
as he gets more powerful.  Once he reaches the highest levels, he has become a
shrunken, wizened and decrepid old thing, kept alive only by continual spells
that restore his dwindeling life force.  So an extremely high level wizard
would have a "restore life" spell of some kind, and he would need to retain
enough magic power so that he would be able to cast the spell when required
on a regular basis (sort of like food, but he would still need food also).
